      "text": "To determine the number of different ways to distribute six identical books such that at least one is in the library and at least one is checked out, we start by considering the possible distributions:\n\n1. **Total Distribution Types**: If all six books were in the library, there is exactly one way to arrange them, but this does not meet our condition of at least one book being checked out. Similarly, if all six were checked out, there is exactly one way to arrange them, again not meeting our condition of having at least one book in the library.\n\n2. **Distributing Books**: We need to distribute books in such a way that at least one book is in the library and at least one is checked out. We'll calculate the total number of distributions and then exclude the cases where all are in the library or all are checked out.\n\nTotal distributions without restrictions include all possible combinations of placing books in the library or checked out. This can be calculated using the stars and bars method, treating the six books as stars and the conditions as the usage of bins. Combinations are represented by \\(\\binom{n+r-1}{n}\\), where \\(n\\) are the books and \\(r\\) is the bins (distributions).\n\nFirst, consider the total number of ways to balance books:\n\\[\n\\text{Bin Choices} = \\frac{6+6}{2} = 6 \\text{ choices} \n\\]\n\nNext, validate all potential distributions (6!) steps with the above distribution:\n\n\\[ \n\\binom{n+r-1}{r} = \\frac{6+6-1}{6+6}, \\text{where} \\ n=6 \\text{and} \\ r=2} \n\\]\n\nThis approach consideration leads to combinations without imaginary disconnections, meeting constraints:\nThus, avoiding all zeros:\n\n\\[ \n\\begin{array}{c} \n1. \\ 6 - 1 \\; \\text{in library} \\\\ \n2. \\ 6 - k \\; \\text{in library for} \\ k \\text{from} \\ 1 \\quad \\text{up to 5} \\\\ \n3. \\ 6 - k+2 \\; \\text{out of library for} \\ k \\text{from} \\ 0 \\quad \\text{up to 4} \n\\end{array} \n\\]\n\nBy computation by Schroeder-Russel’s (strictly explained variations), books, given different distributions without rotinas displacement:\n\nPokécatu ensures constrained 5!\n\nFinal result:\n\\boxed{51}",
